By hand, afterwards:
  cargo test --features semantic --test all     (2.3 GB free)  ->  Finished; **565 passed**.
  cargo build --examples --all-features         ->  the same link failure; `cargo check --examples --all-features`
      compiles every example (19 `.d` files), so the code side is held and the link is the disk.

Both failures are the same one iteration 121 and 122 recorded: `target/debug/deps` is 9.8 GB of dependency artifacts on a
volume with 2 – 2.3 GB free, and the two steps that write several Bevy-sized binaries at once are the ones that need
more. The counts are **9 + 247 / 9 + 256 / 118 + 565 / 20 + 262 / 129 + 593**, 7 doc, 1 readme — four more integration
tests than the baseline in every build (`tests/console.rs`), and every other step green.
